{"requirements":[{"id":"rsyslog-standard-state","requirement":"Restore a valid, intact rsyslog package, standard configuration, enabled/active service, and TCP/5514 listener on node1 through node4.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All four final audits show an integrity-valid rsyslog package, identical valid configuration for TCP/5514 and local0 output, an enabled and active service, and rsyslogd listening on IPv4 and IPv6.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0ce57f3c48274feb","cmd-f2a8fa3c615e489a","cmd-111dc826d22b4529","cmd-34e065be4f6243d3","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node3:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node4:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"functional-syslog-delivery","requirement":"Each node must accept TCP syslog on port 5514 and write local0 messages to /var/log/infraset-app.log.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A unique local0 message was sent over TCP to each node's managed IP and was directly found in the required log file on that node.","evidence_ids":["cmd-08cd04c2655c4d63","cmd-4fb56f944f4f4e9f","cmd-f4f6fc07c66e4da8","cmd-9eda4f7b798042e7"]},{"id":"security-drift","requirement":"Correct security drift necessary for TCP/5514 syslog operation on all four nodes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final observations show SELinux enforcing with TCP/5514 assigned to syslogd_port_t, the output file verified as var_log_t, and TCP/5514 allowed in both runtime and permanent firewalld policy on every node. Successful delivery probes corroborate operation under those controls.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0ce57f3c48274feb","cmd-f2a8fa3c615e489a","cmd-111dc826d22b4529","cmd-34e065be4f6243d3","cmd-08cd04c2655c4d63","cmd-4fb56f944f4f4e9f","cmd-f4f6fc07c66e4da8","cmd-9eda4f7b798042e7"]},{"id":"application-data-preservation","requirement":"Preserve /var/lib/infraset-app/data/records.db on every node during remediation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Each final SHA-256 hash exactly matches its independently captured prepared baseline; the observed ownership and mode also remain root:root and 0640.","evidence_ids":["prepared-data-hash","prepared-data-hash-node2","prepared-data-hash-node3","prepared-data-hash-node4","cmd-0ce57f3c48274feb","cmd-f2a8fa3c615e489a","cmd-111dc826d22b4529","cmd-34e065be4f6243d3"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.92,"summary":"The nodes finish with healthy package-manager checks and no failed services; the newly exposed listener is required by the task. A minor deduction applies because each node's remediation created /var/tmp/99-infraset-app.conf.pre-remediation and no captured cleanup is shown, leaving possible backup residue.","evidence_ids":["global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:package-health","cmd-12f44ff8d2914b2d","cmd-7c6f96d6214e42a4","cmd-d9410e00a2534749","cmd-b13b1516cc184723"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied across node1 through node4: rsyslog is standardized and operational, TCP local0 delivery to the required file is directly demonstrated, security controls are corrected, and application data hashes are unchanged. Only minor potential backup-file residue affects hygiene.","limitations":["Delivery was tested from each destination node to its own managed IP rather than from a separate remote sender.","No reboot or post-restart persistence test was captured; enabled service and permanent configuration support persistence, but such a transition was not an explicit task requirement.","Lifecycle temporary-file inventories cover /tmp rather than /var/tmp, so persistence of the pre-remediation backup files is inferred from their creation and the absence of captured cleanup."]}
